<title>BELGIUM: ROYALE BELGE/BANK IPPA TO TRIM MORTGAGE RATES.</title>
<headline>ROYALE BELGE/BANK IPPA TO TRIM MORTGAGE RATES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian insurer Royale Belge and</p>
<p>its banking unit Bank Ippa said they would trim their mortgage</p>
<p>lending rates by 0.25 percentage with immediate effect.</p>
<p>The move was a reaction to lower market interest</p>
<p>rates, Royale Belge said in a statement.</p>
<p>The move comes after several other Belgian lenders also</p>
<p>reduced their mortgage rates.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
